      "scientific_notes": [
        "Under compound symmetry with k repeated measures, the variance of the subject-level average is \u03c3\u00b2/k where \u03c3\u00b2 is the marginal variance.",
        "The effective SD for the group comparison at the subject-level is \u03c3_avg = \u03c3 / \u221ak = 2.5 / \u221a3.",
        "This reduces to a two-sample t-test with pooled SD = \u03c3_avg * \u221a2 = 2.5 * \u221a(2/3).",
        "The effect size (Cohen's d) is \u03b4 = (\u03bc1 - \u03bc2) / \u03c3_pooled = 2 / (2.5 * \u221a(2/3))."
      ]
    },
